{
  "title": "Expand ingredient categorizer keyword coverage",
  "description": "data/ingredients.json has 640 keyword-to-category mappings. \
Measured against data/unique-ingredients.txt (16,411 historical parsed \
ingredient strings), ~10.7% of items fall through to 'Other'. The misses split \
into two buckets:\n\
\n\
1. Genuine vocabulary gaps: marshmallows, dulce de leche, pie filling, \
applesauce, candy melting wafers, chili beans, simple syrup, plain 'water', \
chocolate morsels, Heath bars, etc.\n\
2. Ingredient-parsing junk that no keyword list can fix ('+ 2 Tbsp warm \
water', '(440-gram) cans', ')'). Don't try to fix these with keywords — file \
separate parser issues if a pattern is common.\n\
\n\
Task: mine the most frequent 'Other' items and add keywords to \
data/ingredients.json until the Other rate is substantially down \
(frequency-weighted). To reproduce the measurement, run the categorizer \
(ramekin-core/src/ingredient_categorizer.rs) over the corpus and tally \
categories.\n\
\n\
Notes:\n\
- The matcher is longest-keyword-first token matching with plural inflection \
(s/es/ies/y), so prefer the shortest distinctive keyword and watch for \
collisions with existing longer keywords (e.g. 'dried basil' vs 'basil').\n\
- data/unique-ingredients.txt is the primary corpus. If \
p2-shopping-list-prod-items-corpus has landed, also cover its (small) \
prod-derived corpus — its main value is hand-typed non-recipe store items \
(household goods etc.), which may motivate adding new categories beyond the \
current food-oriented 16 (e.g. Household, Personal Care). Adding a category \
touches the hardcoded lists in web and iOS too (see \
p3-shopping-list-category-order-from-api).\n\
- Keep the existing unit tests in ingredient_categorizer.rs green; add tests \
for newly handled tricky cases.\n\
\n\
Findings from p2-shopping-list-prod-items-corpus (landed): the prod corpus is \
data/shopping-list-categories.json (280 distinct items as {item, count, \
category} with expected-category labels); `make \
shopping-list-categorizer-test` scores the categorizer over it (currently \
82.1% accuracy, 10.4% 'Other', 20 coverage gaps). Out-of-taxonomy items that \
fall to 'Other' and may motivate NEW categories: dish soap, 'Palmolive ultra \
strength', dishwasher detergent (Household/Cleaning); Ibuprofen \
(Pharmacy/Personal Care); dog treats (Pet); plus prepared/junk entries 'Cold \
salad', 'Dip', 'Go humans'. Recurring breakfast-cereal gap (Chex / Rice Chex / \
Wheat Chex / corn Chex / Lucky Charms / M&Ms) — no Snacks/Cereal keyword \
catches them. Recipe-derived keyword targets the corpus surfaced: fresh citrus \
'lemon/lime juice' -> Beverages (should be Produce), 'frozen \
strawberries'/'french fries' miss 'frozen', pickled/fermented \
'Sauerkraut'+'Kimchi' -> Other, and snack forms (potato/tortilla chips, \
pretzel twists) matching their base ingredient instead of Snacks.",
  "status": "open",
